<title>BRAZIL: Nokia, Gradiente to build Brazil plant.</title>
<headline>Nokia, Gradiente to build Brazil plant.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish telecom giant Nokia and local electronics company Gradiente Eletronica S.A. will form a joint venture to build a cellular telephone factory in Brazil, Gradiente said.</p>
<p>The firm said in a statement that Gradiente President Eugenio Staub and Nokia's executive vice president for the Americas, Olli Kallasvuo, will formalize a joint-venture agreement Thursday.</p>
<p>The two plan to hold a news conference afterwards to provide details on the deal.</p>
<p>((--James Craig, Sao Paulo newsroom 5511 2485413))</p>
